 ],
 "notes": "Role names are not in the prompt, so the control-plane and nodes roles (both assumable only by EC2) cannot be told apart; policy checks require attachment to some EC2-assumable role, and to the controllers role (the one also trusting pods.eks.amazonaws.com) where the prompt names it. 'Attached to both roles' accepts one policy with >=2 Roles or separate per-role policies. Specific grants use glob_covers (so eks:*/ec2:*/* also satisfy); each policy selector has a list-Action and a string-Action variant, so a single policy mixing string and list Action statements would not match. Read-only console policy: every action must be Describe*/List*/Get*/AccessKubernetesApi. Limitation: 'without attaching it to any role' only checks the policy's own Roles is absent; a role attaching it via ManagedPolicyArns is not detected (no negative ref). Reviewer: controller/EKS policy attachment accepts any EC2-assumable role (the pods-trust miss is scored once, by controllers_role_eks_pods, not cascaded); controllers policy accepts any ec2/autoscaling/elasticloadbalancing actions plus a launch-template and service-linked-role grant; 'related IAM and KMS operations' accepts any iam:/kms: action. The 'two roles' checks also accept >=2 EC2 roles attaching template-defined managed policies via ManagedPolicyArns (the policy->role direction can't be counted)."
